# Android services stubbed in the container on the TouchPad (tenderloin-halium, 16.0 GSI); see
# meta-android's 50-stub-services.
#
# lmkd aborts before main(), in the static constructor of libmemevents.so (the eBPF memory-event
# library), on this 3.4 kernel, and init treats it as critical: "critical process 'lmkd' exited 4 times
# before boot completed", InitFatalReboot, and the container is gone 30 s after it starts (7 Oct 2026).
# LuneOS does not use Android's low-memory killer; the host manages memory.
/system/bin/lmkd
#
# adbd: LuneOS's own adbd serves adb over FunctionFS (android-gadget-setup). The Android 9 image's
# init.tenderloin.usb.rc mounts a second FunctionFS instance in the container and init.usb.rc starts
# /system/bin/adbd on it for sys.usb.config=adb (persist.sys.usb.config=adb in its default.prop).
# android.c has one FunctionFS slot: whichever adbd writes its descriptors last takes the function,
# and the other one closing ep0 unbinds it.
/system/bin/adbd
